{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03605",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.36,
      "end_seconds": 7.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.75,
      "text": "Um, you know, hello? Doctor? I was told to come in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.71,
      "end_seconds": 12.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "No problem at all, come in. What's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 13.27,
      "end_seconds": 17.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "Doctor, I'm just here to help with the details."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 19.22,
      "end_seconds": 25.2,
      "duration_seconds": 5.98,
      "text": "Doctor, um, it's no symptoms. It's getting on my nerves now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.74,
      "end_seconds": 28.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.47,
      "end_seconds": 40.08,
      "duration_seconds": 9.61,
      "text": "Okay, so I'm not sure when it began, to be honest. Some weeks ago, but I can't say how many."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.06,
      "end_seconds": 45.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Would you say mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.83,
      "end_seconds": 48.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "I'd say mild."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.89,
      "end_seconds": 55.42,
      "duration_seconds": 6.53,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 55.52,
      "end_seconds": 63.16,
      "duration_seconds": 7.64,
      "text": "Well, you know, tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.01,
      "end_seconds": 75.44,
      "duration_seconds": 8.43,
      "text": "I mean, I was getting to that! I've also had a low blood count on a routine test."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.19,
      "end_seconds": 80.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Any weight loss, blood in the stool or black stools?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.18,
      "end_seconds": 97.34,
      "duration_seconds": 15.16,
      "text": "No, no weight loss, no blood in the stool, no black stools. I did have slightly tired at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.79,
      "end_seconds": 100.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Any sign of heavy periods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.84,
      "end_seconds": 106.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Nope, uh, no heavy periods."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.21,
      "end_seconds": 109.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.18,
      "end_seconds": 113.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "No, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.8,
      "end_seconds": 118.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Alright, has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.37,
      "end_seconds": 135.76,
      "duration_seconds": 16.39,
      "text": "I've had acid reflux for five years now. I just want to get back to normal, really. Sorry, what was I saying, I've got anxiety. It's the not knowing that gets to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.8,
      "end_seconds": 145.85,
      "duration_seconds": 8.05,
      "text": "Okay, I can see acid reflux in your file as well. Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.45,
      "end_seconds": 158.88,
      "duration_seconds": 12.43,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago. I'm vegetarian and have been for years. Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.17,
      "end_seconds": 163.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Does your family have any medical conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.92,
      "end_seconds": 168.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "My daughter has type 1 diabetes. My grandmother had dementia."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.53,
      "end_seconds": 178.7,
      "duration_seconds": 8.17,
      "text": "Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment? These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.72,
      "end_seconds": 194.36,
      "duration_seconds": 10.64,
      "text": "I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.42,
      "end_seconds": 209.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 210.52,
      "end_seconds": 213.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "He takes pantoprazole, 40 milligrams, before breakfast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.04,
      "end_seconds": 219.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "And for how long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 221.04,
      "end_seconds": 237.27,
      "duration_seconds": 16.23,
      "text": "About two years. Well, uh, he is on escitalopram, 10 milligrams, once a day, I give it to him. He is on ibuprofen, 400 milligrams, most days, I give it to him."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.23,
      "end_seconds": 240.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "Right, I'll do your observations first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.71,
      "end_seconds": 257.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "So, that's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.84,
      "end_seconds": 275.95,
      "duration_seconds": 8.11,
      "text": "Okay: respiratory rate 17, temp 36.7 degrees. And heart rate 78, BP is 110 over 78."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 276.9,
      "end_seconds": 278.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.5,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.79,
      "end_seconds": 281.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "We'll go over that shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.06,
      "end_seconds": 287.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "Right, let's have a proper look at you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 298.0,
      "end_seconds": 299.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.0,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.86,
      "end_seconds": 303.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.91,
      "end_seconds": 320.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "Your pulse and blood pressure are normal, and the eyelids are pale."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 321.81,
      "end_seconds": 322.51,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.29,
      "end_seconds": 360.93,
      "duration_seconds": 34.64,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again. Right, here's what I'm thinking. It points towards iron-deficiency anaemia needing a source found. Another possibility is a stomach ulcer from tablets. Another possibility is a bowel cancer. What I'm giving you is ferrous sulfate, 200 milligrams, once a day, three months. You take it by mouth. That's for iron deficiency. Let's plan a check after the tests. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 362.97,
      "end_seconds": 366.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "Great, thank you for your help."
    }
  ]
}